Rule 3 (tensor must be non-empty and contain only positive values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (input tensors must have compatible dimensions for matrix multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0))
>>
Rule 5 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 8 (input tensor must contain only non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) ≥ 0
